1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:02,189
This video is about one paper:

2
00:00:02,239 --> 00:00:07,222
Few-step cofolding with all-atom flow maps, from Genesis Molecular AI, with

3
00:00:07,272 --> 00:00:11,910
collaborators at MIT, Carnegie Mellon, Imperial College and Mila.

4
00:00:11,960 --> 00:00:13,784
The method is called DeCAF.

5
00:00:15,200 --> 00:00:20,352
Cofolding models, like AlphaFold 3 or Boltz, predict a protein together with the

6
00:00:20,402 --> 00:00:22,134
small molecule bound to it.

7
00:00:22,184 --> 00:00:26,960
Their last stage is a diffusion model over the coordinates of every atom, and

8
00:00:27,010 --> 00:00:31,936
producing a single structure means running that diffusion module about two hundred

9
00:00:31,986 --> 00:00:32,457
times.

10
00:00:33,033 --> 00:00:35,926
DeCAF distills such a model into a flow map:

11
00:00:35,976 --> 00:00:41,144
a network that, instead of walking along the denoising trajectory in small steps,

12
00:00:41,194 --> 00:00:42,194
jumps along it.

13
00:00:42,244 --> 00:00:45,794
The same network can take one jump, or five, or ten.

14
00:00:46,867 --> 00:00:48,789
Flow maps themselves are not new.

15
00:00:48,839 --> 00:00:53,387
The contribution is making them work for an all-atom teacher of the EDM kind, and

16
00:00:53,437 --> 00:00:55,360
it comes down to three decisions.

17
00:00:55,410 --> 00:00:58,820
First, index the flow map by noise level instead of time.

18
00:00:58,870 --> 00:01:03,212
Second, parameterize it as a denoiser, so that the training loss compares

19
00:01:03,262 --> 00:01:07,633
structures and can be rigidly aligned, exactly like the teacher's own loss.

20
00:01:07,683 --> 00:01:11,825
Third, use the map's cheap look-ahead to guide search at inference time.

21
00:01:11,875 --> 00:01:13,293
Let's take them in order.

22
00:01:13,867 --> 00:01:15,324
First, the teacher.

23
00:01:15,374 --> 00:01:19,022
Stack all the atom coordinates into one long vector, x.

24
00:01:19,072 --> 00:01:21,936
The noising process is variance exploding:

25
00:01:21,986 --> 00:01:27,083
x sigma equals the clean structure, x zero, plus sigma times standard Gaussian

26
00:01:27,133 --> 00:01:27,611
noise.

27
00:01:27,661 --> 00:01:32,607
In Boltz, sigma ranges from under a hundredth of an angstrom to about two and a

28
00:01:32,657 --> 00:01:34,246
half thousand angstroms.

29
00:01:34,800 --> 00:01:39,818
The network is a denoiser, D of x and sigma, which predicts the clean structure.

30
00:01:39,868 --> 00:01:42,251
Ideally, it is the posterior mean:

31
00:01:42,301 --> 00:01:45,446
the expected clean structure, given the noisy one.

32
00:01:46,000 --> 00:01:51,355
Sampling integrates the probability flow ODE, or a stochastic version of it.

33
00:01:51,405 --> 00:01:56,869
Written directly in terms of the noise level, the ODE is remarkably simple:

34
00:01:56,919 --> 00:02:00,445
d x, d sigma, equals x minus D, over sigma.

35
00:02:00,495 --> 00:02:04,184
We'll call the right-hand side the sigma velocity, v.

36
00:02:04,767 --> 00:02:07,026
Here is a picture we'll use throughout.

37
00:02:07,076 --> 00:02:09,557
The horizontal axis is the noise level:

38
00:02:09,607 --> 00:02:12,593
pure noise on the left, clean data on the right.

39
00:02:12,643 --> 00:02:16,399
The vertical axis is a one-dimensional stand-in for the structure.

40
00:02:16,449 --> 00:02:21,072
The data distribution has two modes; think of two different binding poses.

41
00:02:21,122 --> 00:02:25,680
Every curve is an exact trajectory of the ODE, carrying a point from the broad

42
00:02:25,730 --> 00:02:28,879
Gaussian on the left to one of the modes on the right.

43
00:02:29,433 --> 00:02:33,981
A standard sampler walks along a trajectory with small Euler steps, one network

44
00:02:34,031 --> 00:02:34,905
call per step.

45
00:02:34,955 --> 00:02:37,280
With many steps, it tracks the curve.

46
00:02:37,330 --> 00:02:41,814
With only five, each step follows the local tangent, the curvature makes it

47
00:02:41,864 --> 00:02:46,524
undershoot, and it ends up between the modes, where there is no data at all.

48
00:02:47,100 --> 00:02:49,094
A flow map skips the walking.

49
00:02:49,144 --> 00:02:54,925
Capital X, sub rho sigma, takes a point at noise level rho, and returns where its

50
00:02:54,975 --> 00:02:58,017
trajectory is at the lower noise level sigma.

51
00:02:58,067 --> 00:03:00,707
It is the solution operator of the ODE.

52
00:03:01,267 --> 00:03:03,050
Two properties pin it down.

53
00:03:03,100 --> 00:03:05,629
Mapping a level to itself does nothing.

54
00:03:05,679 --> 00:03:07,021
And maps compose:

55
00:03:07,071 --> 00:03:11,874
going from rho to sigma and then on to tau is the same as going from rho to tau

56
00:03:11,924 --> 00:03:12,601
directly.

57
00:03:12,651 --> 00:03:17,031
A consistency model is the special case that only ever jumps to zero.

58
00:03:17,081 --> 00:03:22,228
A flow map can jump between any two levels, so one network supports any number of

59
00:03:22,278 --> 00:03:22,763
steps.

60
00:03:23,333 --> 00:03:27,313
To learn it, you need a differential equation that it satisfies.

61
00:03:27,363 --> 00:03:29,944
The Lagrangian view moves the end point:

62
00:03:29,994 --> 00:03:34,504
the derivative of X with respect to the target level is the velocity at the end

63
00:03:34,554 --> 00:03:35,004
point.

64
00:03:35,054 --> 00:03:38,116
The Eulerian view moves the starting point instead.

65
00:03:38,667 --> 00:03:43,557
Slide the start along its own trajectory, and the destination does not move.

66
00:03:43,607 --> 00:03:48,854
So the derivative with respect to rho, taken along the velocity field, is zero.

67
00:03:48,904 --> 00:03:53,956
This is the equation the released DeCAF code enforces, with the teacher's velocity

68
00:03:54,006 --> 00:03:54,894
as the field.

69
00:03:55,467 --> 00:03:59,818
Before that can work, there is a problem that looks like bookkeeping, but turns out

70
00:03:59,868 --> 00:04:00,728
to matter a lot.

71
00:04:01,100 --> 00:04:06,248
Generic flow map recipes are written in a time variable, t, between zero and one.

72
00:04:06,298 --> 00:04:11,180
The teacher lives in noise level, and the two are connected by the schedule it was

73
00:04:11,230 --> 00:04:12,255
trained with:

74
00:04:12,305 --> 00:04:17,300
a Karras schedule, which interpolates linearly in sigma to the power one seventh.

75
00:04:17,867 --> 00:04:20,771
Changing variables brings in the chain rule.

76
00:04:20,821 --> 00:04:24,826
The velocity in t is the sigma velocity times d sigma, d t.

77
00:04:24,876 --> 00:04:30,103
For this schedule, d sigma d t is about a quarter of an angstrom per unit time at

78
00:04:30,153 --> 00:04:34,179
the clean end, and about fifteen thousand at the noisy end.

79
00:04:34,229 --> 00:04:38,830
That is a factor of sixty thousand, almost five orders of magnitude.

80
00:04:39,400 --> 00:04:42,385
Now look at what the Eulerian objective needs.

81
00:04:42,435 --> 00:04:47,595
It regresses onto the teacher's velocity, and it differentiates the network along

82
00:04:47,645 --> 00:04:52,548
the trajectory, which is a Jacobian-vector product whose tangent is that same

83
00:04:52,598 --> 00:04:53,280
velocity.

84
00:04:53,330 --> 00:04:57,047
In time coordinates, both carry the factor d sigma d t.

85
00:04:57,097 --> 00:05:02,365
Depending on where the pair of times lands, the targets and the derivatives change

86
00:05:02,415 --> 00:05:05,325
scale by up to that factor of sixty thousand.

87
00:05:05,375 --> 00:05:10,317
The paper reports that time-parameterized objectives become numerically unstable

88
00:05:10,367 --> 00:05:11,348
because of it.

89
00:05:11,900 --> 00:05:13,967
The fix is a change of variables.

90
00:05:14,017 --> 00:05:18,937
Index the flow map by noise levels directly, and write every objective and every

91
00:05:18,987 --> 00:05:20,469
sampling step in sigma.

92
00:05:20,519 --> 00:05:25,541
The sigma velocity is just the teacher's noise prediction, so it is of order one at

93
00:05:25,591 --> 00:05:26,775
every noise level.

94
00:05:26,825 --> 00:05:30,876
The tangent of the Jacobian-vector product is simply v, and one.

95
00:05:30,926 --> 00:05:33,229
The factor d sigma d t never appears.

96
00:05:33,279 --> 00:05:37,939
The schedule survives only as a choice of which noise levels to train on and to

97
00:05:37,989 --> 00:05:38,875
step through.

98
00:05:39,433 --> 00:05:40,715
Second decision:

99
00:05:40,765 --> 00:05:42,603
how to parameterize the map.

100
00:05:42,653 --> 00:05:47,772
Start from the simplest possible jump, one Euler step of the ODE from rho down to

101
00:05:47,822 --> 00:05:48,305
sigma.

102
00:05:48,355 --> 00:05:51,477
For this process, that is exactly a DDIM step.

103
00:05:51,527 --> 00:05:54,961
Rearranged, the new point is a weighted average:

104
00:05:55,011 --> 00:06:00,262
sigma over rho times the current point, plus one minus sigma over rho, times the

105
00:06:00,312 --> 00:06:01,546
denoised estimate.

106
00:06:02,100 --> 00:06:05,622
In our picture, this has a clean geometric meaning.

107
00:06:05,672 --> 00:06:09,635
An Euler step moves along the tangent line of the trajectory.

108
00:06:09,685 --> 00:06:14,811
And the tangent line at level rho crosses the clean axis, sigma equals zero,

109
00:06:14,861 --> 00:06:17,003
exactly at the denoiser's output.

110
00:06:17,053 --> 00:06:20,583
The teacher's denoiser is where the tangent line lands.

111
00:06:21,133 --> 00:06:26,227
DeCAF keeps this form, but lets the denoiser know where the jump is going.

112
00:06:26,277 --> 00:06:31,639
X rho sigma of x equals sigma over rho times x, plus one minus sigma over rho,

113
00:06:31,689 --> 00:06:34,625
times D theta of x, rho, and sigma:

114
00:06:34,675 --> 00:06:37,319
a denoiser that takes two noise levels.

115
00:06:37,900 --> 00:06:42,934
Geometrically, the exact flow map lands on the trajectory, not on the tangent.

116
00:06:42,984 --> 00:06:47,982
Draw the chord from the starting point through that landing point, and extend it to

117
00:06:48,032 --> 00:06:49,012
the clean axis.

118
00:06:49,062 --> 00:06:52,267
Where it crosses is exactly what D theta must output.

119
00:06:52,317 --> 00:06:54,777
The tangent gives the teacher's denoiser.

120
00:06:54,827 --> 00:06:57,216
The chord gives the flow map's denoiser.

121
00:06:57,767 --> 00:06:59,757
Three properties come for free.

122
00:06:59,807 --> 00:07:04,943
When sigma equals rho, the map is the identity, whatever the network outputs.

123
00:07:04,993 --> 00:07:10,514
As sigma approaches rho, the chord turns into the tangent, so the diagonal, D theta

124
00:07:10,564 --> 00:07:14,177
of x, rho, rho, must equal the teacher's denoiser.

125
00:07:14,227 --> 00:07:19,442
That is the tangent condition, and training it is ordinary denoiser distillation.

126
00:07:19,492 --> 00:07:24,011
And at sigma equals zero, the chord ends at the trajectory's end point.

127
00:07:24,061 --> 00:07:29,163
So a single network call, from any noise level, returns a sharp clean structure

128
00:07:29,213 --> 00:07:31,078
rather than a posterior mean.

129
00:07:31,633 --> 00:07:36,017
In the released code, the student has the same architecture as the teacher's

130
00:07:36,067 --> 00:07:39,363
diffusion module, plus a second noise-level embedding.

131
00:07:39,413 --> 00:07:44,159
The Pairformer trunk and the teacher are frozen, and only this head is trained.

132
00:07:44,733 --> 00:07:45,614
Now the loss.

133
00:07:45,664 --> 00:07:48,529
Write the jump with an average velocity, u.

134
00:07:48,579 --> 00:07:54,228
X equals x, minus rho minus sigma, times u, where u is x minus D theta, over rho.

135
00:07:54,278 --> 00:07:58,815
Substituting into the Eulerian equation gives an identity that the exact map

136
00:07:58,865 --> 00:07:59,752
satisfies:

137
00:07:59,802 --> 00:08:05,186
u equals v, minus rho minus sigma, times the derivative of u along the trajectory.

138
00:08:05,236 --> 00:08:10,492
That derivative costs one Jacobian-vector product, in the direction v in space, and

139
00:08:10,542 --> 00:08:11,300
one in rho.

140
00:08:11,867 --> 00:08:16,318
So the student regresses u, plus rho minus sigma times the stop-gradient

141
00:08:16,368 --> 00:08:19,043
derivative, onto the teacher's velocity.

142
00:08:19,093 --> 00:08:24,635
On the diagonal, where sigma equals rho, the correction vanishes, and this is plain

143
00:08:24,685 --> 00:08:26,148
denoiser distillation.

144
00:08:26,700 --> 00:08:28,007
Here is the key step.

145
00:08:28,057 --> 00:08:29,842
Multiply the residual by rho.

146
00:08:29,892 --> 00:08:32,204
Both sides turn into clean structures.

147
00:08:32,254 --> 00:08:37,635
On one side, the student's clean prediction, corrected by the derivative term; call

148
00:08:37,685 --> 00:08:38,295
it D hat.

149
00:08:38,345 --> 00:08:41,587
On the other side, the teacher's denoised structure.

150
00:08:41,637 --> 00:08:46,289
The loss becomes a distance between two point clouds, weighted by one over rho

151
00:08:46,339 --> 00:08:46,909
squared.

152
00:08:47,467 --> 00:08:48,836
Why does that matter?

153
00:08:48,886 --> 00:08:52,385
AlphaFold-style networks are not built to be equivariant.

154
00:08:52,435 --> 00:08:57,454
They are trained with random rotations, and with a loss that first rigidly aligns

155
00:08:57,504 --> 00:08:59,845
the ground truth onto the prediction.

156
00:08:59,895 --> 00:09:04,735
So nothing in the teacher's training loss depends on the global orientation of its

157
00:09:04,785 --> 00:09:05,317
output.

158
00:09:05,367 --> 00:09:10,227
Boltz's own sampler even re-aligns the noisy coordinates to the denoised prediction

159
00:09:10,277 --> 00:09:11,471
before every step.

160
00:09:12,033 --> 00:09:16,456
A velocity-matching loss would ask the student to reproduce that arbitrary pose.

161
00:09:16,506 --> 00:09:20,724
Those residuals can be large and systematic, and they say nothing about the

162
00:09:20,774 --> 00:09:21,420
structure.

163
00:09:21,470 --> 00:09:25,039
In structure space, you can do what the teacher's loss did:

164
00:09:25,089 --> 00:09:29,588
find the best rigid motion with the Kabsch algorithm, weighted toward the ligand

165
00:09:29,638 --> 00:09:34,131
atoms, align the teacher's structure onto the student's, and only then take the

166
00:09:34,181 --> 00:09:34,883
difference.

167
00:09:34,933 --> 00:09:37,098
What remains is the part that matters.

168
00:09:37,667 --> 00:09:42,573
The paper reports that this alignment substantially reduces gradient variance, and

169
00:09:42,623 --> 00:09:44,630
that it is critical for accuracy.

170
00:09:44,680 --> 00:09:48,319
The teacher's smooth LDDT loss carries over unchanged, too.

171
00:09:48,369 --> 00:09:50,014
So one training step is:

172
00:09:50,064 --> 00:09:55,123
draw two noise levels from the teacher's schedule, noise a training structure, make

173
00:09:55,173 --> 00:10:00,049
one teacher call and one student call with its Jacobian-vector product, and take an

174
00:10:00,099 --> 00:10:02,057
aligned loss in structure space.

175
00:10:02,633 --> 00:10:05,033
Sampling with the trained map is simple.

176
00:10:05,083 --> 00:10:09,628
Deterministically, you chain jumps along a short schedule of noise levels.

177
00:10:09,678 --> 00:10:15,019
Five jumps, five network calls, and in this toy, with an exact map, the end points

178
00:10:15,069 --> 00:10:17,631
land on the data, not between the modes.

179
00:10:18,200 --> 00:10:22,995
DeCAF also uses gamma sampling, a knob between determinism and fresh noise.

180
00:10:23,045 --> 00:10:28,514
Jump to a slightly lower level, sigma tilde, equal to root one minus gamma squared,

181
00:10:28,564 --> 00:10:29,392
times sigma.

182
00:10:29,442 --> 00:10:32,247
Then add gamma sigma worth of Gaussian noise.

183
00:10:32,297 --> 00:10:34,731
The total noise level is back to sigma.

184
00:10:34,781 --> 00:10:37,215
Gamma equals zero is the pure flow map.

185
00:10:37,265 --> 00:10:41,831
Gamma equals one jumps all the way to a clean structure and re-noises, like

186
00:10:41,881 --> 00:10:43,872
multistep consistency sampling.

187
00:10:44,433 --> 00:10:45,672
Third decision:

188
00:10:45,722 --> 00:10:47,406
search at inference time.

189
00:10:47,456 --> 00:10:52,661
Boltz-1x steers sampling with physics-based potentials, penalizing clashes, bad

190
00:10:52,711 --> 00:10:54,965
bond geometry and wrong chirality.

191
00:10:55,015 --> 00:11:00,183
To score a noisy intermediate state, the potential is evaluated on the denoiser's

192
00:11:00,233 --> 00:11:01,046
prediction.

193
00:11:01,600 --> 00:11:04,014
But a denoiser returns a posterior mean.

194
00:11:04,064 --> 00:11:08,864
At high noise, that is an average over very different outcomes, and it can sit

195
00:11:08,914 --> 00:11:12,026
between the modes, where no real structure lives.

196
00:11:12,076 --> 00:11:14,817
The reward of the mean is not the mean reward.

197
00:11:15,400 --> 00:11:19,608
The flow map's full jump lands where the trajectory actually ends:

198
00:11:19,658 --> 00:11:23,274
a concrete structure, for the same single network call.

199
00:11:23,324 --> 00:11:25,848
The paper calls this an exact look-ahead.

200
00:11:25,898 --> 00:11:31,007
Exact with respect to the probability flow, and only as good as the learned map.

201
00:11:31,567 --> 00:11:34,129
DeCAF-Search is built around that look-ahead.

202
00:11:34,179 --> 00:11:36,048
Keep a population of particles.

203
00:11:36,098 --> 00:11:41,118
At each noise level, look ahead with the flow map, refine the clean prediction with

204
00:11:41,168 --> 00:11:45,690
reward gradients, re-noise to the next level, and reallocate compute with a

205
00:11:45,740 --> 00:11:46,699
selection rule.

206
00:11:47,267 --> 00:11:50,138
The choice of rule recovers familiar methods.

207
00:11:50,188 --> 00:11:54,929
Resampling in proportion to exponentiated reward gives Feynman-Kac steering.

208
00:11:54,979 --> 00:11:59,131
An upper-confidence rule over a tree gives Monte Carlo tree search.

209
00:11:59,181 --> 00:12:03,762
Never reallocating, and keeping the best at the end, gives best-of-N.

210
00:12:03,812 --> 00:12:06,876
One algorithm, spanning every compute budget.

211
00:12:07,433 --> 00:12:08,664
What does this buy?

212
00:12:08,714 --> 00:12:13,575
For DeCAF-Boltz, distilled from Boltz-1, the paper reports near-parity with the

213
00:12:13,625 --> 00:12:16,960
teacher at about five times fewer network evaluations.

214
00:12:17,010 --> 00:12:21,776
At tight budgets of ten to fifty evaluations, it beats Boltz-1x run at the same

215
00:12:21,826 --> 00:12:24,920
budget, on both accuracy and physical validity.

216
00:12:24,970 --> 00:12:30,029
And on PoseBusters, it matches the full-budget, six-hundred-evaluation Boltz-1x,

217
00:12:30,079 --> 00:12:32,515
with roughly twenty times less compute.

218
00:12:33,067 --> 00:12:35,681
Here is the headline benchmark:

219
00:12:35,731 --> 00:12:41,128
Runs N' Poses, complexes released after 2023, best of five samples.

220
00:12:41,178 --> 00:12:46,917
Success means a ligand RMSD under two angstroms, and passing the PoseBusters

221
00:12:46,967 --> 00:12:48,285
validity checks.

222
00:12:48,867 --> 00:12:53,606
The Pearl teacher, at full budget, scores seventy-eight point three.

223
00:12:53,656 --> 00:12:56,643
The distilled DeCAF-Pearl scores seventy-seven.

224
00:12:56,693 --> 00:13:01,663
DeCAF-Boltz scores sixty-six point eight, level with Boltz-1x at sixty-six point

225
00:13:01,713 --> 00:13:02,143
nine.

226
00:13:02,193 --> 00:13:03,247
AlphaFold 3:

227
00:13:03,297 --> 00:13:04,680
sixty-nine point six.

228
00:13:04,730 --> 00:13:05,404
Chai-1:

229
00:13:05,454 --> 00:13:06,903
sixty-two point three.

230
00:13:06,953 --> 00:13:07,692
Boltz-2:

231
00:13:07,742 --> 00:13:09,060
sixty-one point six.

232
00:13:09,633 --> 00:13:10,882
Read this carefully.

233
00:13:10,932 --> 00:13:15,806
Relative to its own teacher, distillation cost about one point, at a fraction of

234
00:13:15,856 --> 00:13:16,644
the compute.

235
00:13:16,694 --> 00:13:18,276
That is the actual result.

236
00:13:18,326 --> 00:13:23,145
The margin over AlphaFold 3, Chai-1 and Boltz-2 comes from the teacher, Pearl,

237
00:13:23,195 --> 00:13:27,200
which is Genesis's own model; it is not created by distillation.

238
00:13:27,250 --> 00:13:29,362
DeCAF-Boltz sits level with Boltz-1x.

239
00:13:29,412 --> 00:13:33,110
What the distilled models do show is high physical validity:

240
00:13:33,160 --> 00:13:35,841
ninety-eight to ninety-nine and a half percent.

241
00:13:36,400 --> 00:13:37,311
To summarize.

242
00:13:37,361 --> 00:13:37,889
One:

243
00:13:37,939 --> 00:13:40,124
index the flow map by noise level.

244
00:13:40,174 --> 00:13:45,062
This removes a schedule-induced factor spanning five orders of magnitude from the

245
00:13:45,112 --> 00:13:46,403
training objective.

246
00:13:46,453 --> 00:13:46,980
Two:

247
00:13:47,030 --> 00:13:49,847
parameterize the map as a two-level denoiser.

248
00:13:49,897 --> 00:13:55,021
This builds in the boundary and tangent conditions, and turns distillation into a

249
00:13:55,071 --> 00:13:59,952
distance between structures, which can be rigidly aligned exactly the way the

250
00:14:00,002 --> 00:14:01,345
teacher was trained.

251
00:14:01,395 --> 00:14:02,049
Three:

252
00:14:02,099 --> 00:14:07,111
use the flow map's look-ahead for reward-guided search, which unifies steering,

253
00:14:07,161 --> 00:14:08,746
tree search and best-of-N.

254
00:14:09,300 --> 00:14:10,335
And the caveats.

255
00:14:10,385 --> 00:14:13,699
This is distillation, so the ceiling is the teacher.

256
00:14:13,749 --> 00:14:16,353
The savings are in the structure module:

257
00:14:16,403 --> 00:14:21,268
the trunk still runs once per complex, so end-to-end speedups depend on system size

258
00:14:21,318 --> 00:14:23,335
and on how many samples you draw.

259
00:14:23,385 --> 00:14:27,497
Training needs Jacobian-vector products through the structure module.

260
00:14:27,547 --> 00:14:30,787
And the look-ahead is only as exact as the learned map.

261
00:14:31,367 --> 00:14:38,139
Within those limits, it is a clean example of a general idea, flow maps, adapted to

262
00:14:38,189 --> 00:14:40,630
a domain with its own geometry.

263
00:14:40,680 --> 00:14:47,323
The paper is arXiv 2606.08375, and the code and the DeCAF-Boltz weights are public.
